## GrahmOS Branding
**Colors:**
- Primary: #2563EB (blue-600)
- Dark: #1E40AF (blue-800)
- Text: #1F2937 (gray-800)
- Success: #10B981 (emerald-500)
- Warning: #F59E0B (amber-500)
- Error: #EF4444 (red-500)

**Typography:**
- Font: Inter (weights: 400, 500, 600, 700)
- Display: 48px
- H1: 36px
- H2: 28px
- Body: 16px

## Code Guidelines
1. Always use the automate.js CLI wrapper for Webflow API calls
2. Store backups in ~/webflow-cli/grahmos-directory/backups/
3. Use environment variables for secrets (never hardcode API tokens)
4. Follow Webflow API v2.0.0 conventions
5. Rate limit: 500ms between API calls

## Available Scripts
- `node automate.js list-all <collection>` - List collection items
- `node automate.js export <collection> <output.json>` - Export data
- `node automate.js import <collection> <input.json>` - Import data
- `node automate.js schema <collection>` - Get collection schema
- `node automate.js bulk-update <collection> <update.json>` - Bulk updates

## File Structure
```
~/webflow-cli/
├── automate.js              # Main CLI tool
├── .env                     # API credentials
├── cursor-webflow-config.json  # Cursor config
└── grahmos-directory/
    ├── backups/            # All backups (10 files)
    ├── templates/          # Category templates
    ├── data/              # Source data
    ├── results/           # Execution logs
    └── scripts/           # Automation scripts
```

## When Making Changes
1. ALWAYS backup before modifications
2. Test in draft mode first
3. Verify changes before publishing
4. Log all actions to results/ directory
5. Update Notion tracker after each phase

## Restore Process
- Collections: `node automate.js import <collection> <backup.json>`
- Pages: Use Webflow API `/pages/{id}/dom` endpoint
- All backups verified and ready (80KB total)

